Figure 3.3 shows Pascal's triangle displayed in two side-by-side versions from rows n = 0 through n = 7.

On the left, the triangle is written using binomial coefficient notation, \binom{n}{k}:
- Row 0 (apex): \binom{0}{0}
- Row 1: \binom{1}{0}, \binom{1}{1}
- Row 2: \binom{2}{0}, \binom{2}{1}, \binom{2}{2}
- Row 3: \binom{3}{0}, \binom{3}{1}, \binom{3}{2}, \binom{3}{3}
- Row 4: \binom{4}{0}, \binom{4}{1}, \binom{4}{2}, \binom{4}{3}, \binom{4}{4}
- Row 5: \binom{5}{0}, \binom{5}{1}, \binom{5}{2}, \binom{5}{3}, \binom{5}{4}, \binom{5}{5}
- Row 6: \binom{6}{0}, \binom{6}{1}, \binom{6}{2}, \binom{6}{3}, \binom{6}{4}, \binom{6}{5}, \binom{6}{6}
- Row 7: \binom{7}{0}, \binom{7}{1}, \binom{7}{2}, \binom{7}{3}, \binom{7}{4}, \binom{7}{5}, \binom{7}{6}, \binom{7}{7}
Ellipses extend diagonally down to the left, straight down from the middle, and diagonally down to the right, indicating the infinite continuation of the pattern.

On the right, the triangle displays the corresponding numerical values for each binomial coefficient:
- Row 0: 1
- Row 1: 1, 1
- Row 2: 1, 2, 1
- Row 3: 1, 3, 3, 1
- Row 4: 1, 4, 6, 4, 1
- Row 5: 1, 5, 10, 10, 5, 1
- Row 6: 1, 6, 15, 20, 15, 6, 1
- Row 7: 1, 7, 21, 35, 35, 21, 7, 1
Similar ellipses extend below row 7.
